    {
        "content": "<p>Oh wow... I never thought for a moment the operator precedence might be like that (is that on purpose? I would understand with <code>==</code> but also with <code>=</code>?). Thanks!<br>\nEven so, any reason that lemma is missing? If it was there, I wouldn't have messed up the precedence either...</p>",
        "id": 590926538,
        "sender_full_name": "Adomas Baliuka",
        "timestamp": 1777164823
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>idk if that's on purpose, I agree it's unexpected. I just looked at the pretty-printed goal and saw it.</p>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"638715\">Adomas Baliuka</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/.60Bool.2Exor.60.20same.20as.20.60.2B.60/near/590926538\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Even so, any reason that lemma is missing?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I think the question should be, why are you adding booleans? Is it because you used a theorem about <code>Ring</code>s on booleans or can you respell your theorems to use xor directly?</p>\n<p>FWIW addition for booleans was added in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib/pull/15004\">!3#15004</a> without any definitional theorems, but I assume such theorems would be welcome.</p>",
        "id": 590927070,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1777165293
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm playing around with convolutions. I defined this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">circ_convolution_bruteforce</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommMonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofFn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">∑</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v1</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v2</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and then did an example with <code>Bool</code> expecting to get <code>xor</code> (which I did get). Then I got tripped up proving this calculation equals another function.</p>\n<p>Should I not have done the example with <code>Bool</code> (but rather <code>ZMod 2</code>? Or something?)  based on some understanding of what <code>Bool</code> should be used for?</p>",
